# TIER3 — New functions for plant sequence variants

These 9 `.m` files are entirely new, written to quantify histone peptides
whose sequences differ from the human reference due to amino acid substitutions
identified by Multiple Sequence Alignment (MSA) of histone FASTA files.

## Modules and their peptide variants

| Module | Residues | Peptide sequences (propionylated + trypsin) |
|--------|----------|---------------------------------------------|
| H3_11_3_8.m | 3-8 | TKQTAR, TKQSAR*, SNQTAR* |
| H3_12_9_17.m | 9-17 | KSTGGKAPR, KSTGGKGPR*, KSHGGKAPR*, ISTGGKAPR* |
| H3_13_18_26.m | 18-26 | KQLATKAAR, KELATKAAR*, TLLATKAAR*, KQLAPKAAR* |
| H3_14_27_40.m | 27-40 | KSAPATGGVKKPHR, KSAPTTGGVKKPHR*, QSAPATGGVKKPHR* |
| H3_06_53_63.m | 53-63 | KYQKSTELLIR (full PTM panel + relocate) |
| H3_16_53_63.m | 53-63 | KYQKSTELLIR, KYQKSTELLNR* |
| H3_17_73_83.m | 73-83 | EIAQDFKTDLR, EIAQDYKTDLR* |
| H3_18_117_128.m | 117-128 | VTIMPKDIQLAR, VTIMPKDVQLAR*, VTIMPKEIQLAR* |
| H3_Snapshot.m | all | Aggregator: collects all TIER3 hDP results per run |

(*) = plant-specific variant not present in human EpiProfile.

## How variants were identified

1. Retrieve histone H3/H4 protein sequences for the target species from
   UniProt/Phytozome.
2. Perform MSA (ClustalW / MUSCLE) against the human H3.1 reference.
3. Apply in-silico propionylation + trypsin digestion to predict the
   observable peptide set.
4. For each substitution-containing peptide, write a new quantification
   module following the upstream H3_XX pattern (see docs/MANUAL.md
   section 7: Anatomy of a quantification module).

## Data flow

Each TIER3 module writes its results to
`histone_layouts/<run>/detail/H3_<id>_<range>.mat`.
H3_Snapshot.m aggregates these into the per-run snapshot used by
OutputTogether.m for the final cohort-level PTM tables.
